we live in an era of increased  uncertainty  crises and ongoing conflicts a stable  sustainable future sometimes seems out  of reach the university of cambridge  the berlin school of public engagement  and open science  the museum of natural history and the  humble university berlin  have recently launched a joint project  to connect young people  scientists and creatives from all over  the globe  the sustainable futures academy we met  anna ross who did a documentary on the  project in fall  2020. the sustainable futures academy  is basically a very crazy idea to start  with namely to  put together researchers and  young generation gen z as we call them  18 to 25 year olds  with creative professionals to create  science communication and public  engagement output  on the topics of sustainable futures so  we asked all of them to come together  and then in  six groups create sound pieces  digital exhibitions poetry  map making comics it was so interesting  to me that i thought everybody has  different  visions of sustainable futures that's  where there's like  futures and not one future but to me  it's  a fulfillment because it's also a  question about how  we how we feel when we engage in  environmental behaviors and how we  collectively as a future proceed forward  so it's about happiness in a sense and i  think that's ultimately what we're  striving for in a sense it's like the  natural path that we're  eventually as a society going towards  the way the academy was set up it's also  very oh it was very open to grow  with the people that were involved with  it i think that's a central aspect of  the academy that everyone kind of  bought into this idea of we're gonna  participate in something  where we don't know if it's even gonna  work  not only do we not know what's going to  come out of the academy  but if something's going to come out at  all you know  there were so many places where it could  not have worked  but it worked get people from different  walks of life  together to think practically and with  all their knowledge and passion that  they  have of solutions of what can we do what  little things  can we do what systemical things can we  do what can we do together  everything that the participants of the  sustainable futures academy created  will be shown on the berlin science week  so you will be able to  again it's all produced remotely so to  digitally  kind of walk with us through that vision  that all these amazing participants  created  the sustainable futures academy and  the co-creative output can change the  world  by inspiring people to dare to try  something that hasn't been done before  where you don't know if it's going to  work  but to still dare to try and put your  passion  and your knowledge forward and to work  together with other people that might  not be from your field or even from your  walk of life to  try and create a better world
 

